The only problem is that the consequences are very severe for a failed
prayer.

You lose 3 points of luck and your god becomes angry. If you pray
before fixing
any of these conditions your god may reduce your wisdom by 3 and reduce
your
experience level by 1. Otherwise he may also randomly curse your
inventry. It
will also increase your gods anger. Which will result in even worse
treatment the
next time. So don't take a failed prayer lightly.

You will not be able to pray again unless you improve your luck and
pacify your god.
For both you need an altar, and sacrifice. Luck can be improved by a
unicorn and
gems but pacifying the god is the tough part. And if you are chaotic,
you can as
well forget about it, till after well into the middle game.

So if you pray when you had a food item and the prayer fails you will
survive till
your food last but you cannot pray anymore. While if you eat the food
and then
pray after you are out of choices, you cannot go any worse if your god
gets angry.

I don't think you have had the bad luck of a failed prayer. It is quite
rare, but if you
keep up with your logic you will have it eventually.

Actually you can live for a long time if you pray after getting weak,
because each
stomach filling gives you about 900 turns, and weak allows you to pray
200
turns earlier. So that you can handle a timeout of about 1100 turns
after a successful prayer.

50% probability is that the timeout will be less than 350, and about
35% of the
remaining will mean that it will be less than 1100 turns. So that you
have about 67% chance
of being within limit. If you pray consecutively while weak you have an
even chance of
succeeding in two consecutive prayers. But still do it only when there
are no other
alternatives, because the consequences are very severe.

